== 4. Verdict ================================================== 
  NOT USABLE. Neither gene is a target on this panel, so the 
  dataset cannot speak to RASSF9 or RASSF10 however good its 
  design is. This is a property of the 1,412-gene Cancer 
  Transcriptome Atlas panel, not of the analysis. 
 
  What would still work, in order of preference: 
    1. a GeoMx WHOLE TRANSCRIPTOME (~18,000 gene) study of 
       melanocytic progression -- none found in a search of the 
       public literature as of October 2026 
    2. single-cell RNA-seq of nevus AND melanoma TISSUE from the 
       same or matched patients -- GSE230574 has nevus tissue but 
       melanoma only as cell lines 
    3. nevus-associated melanoma specimens, where benign and 
       malignant melanocytes sit in ONE section and share a 
       patient, removing between-patient variation entirely 
    4. laser-capture microdissection of melanocytic nests, which 
       is what GSE112509 already did -- and is why GSE112509 is 
       the more trustworthy of the two bulk cohorts 
 
  Option 3 is the one to put to Gustavo: a within-patient 
  comparison in nevus-associated melanoma would settle this, and 
  such specimens exist in any dermatopathology archive. 
